NAME
     nc - read and write over a connection

SYNOPSIS
     nc [-u] [-v] [-n] [-w SEC] HOST PORT
     nc -l [-u] [-v] PORT

DESCRIPTION
     nc connects to HOST on PORT and copies standard input to it and what
     comes back to standard output. With -l it listens instead. It is
     the simplest way to test that something is listening, or to move a
     file between two machines.

OPTIONS
     -l        listen rather than connect
     -u        UDP rather than TCP
     -v        say what it is doing
     -n        no name lookups
     -w SEC    give up after SEC seconds

SEE ALSO
     curl(1), wget(1), netstat(1)
